   ("P3_TUTOR", "So, your case study is the Lanternfall board game campaign. Remind me why you picked a crowdfunding failure rather than a success."),
   ("P3_TOM", "Most of the module readings are success stories, and we felt that..."),
   ("P3_LEAH", "Tom felt. I wanted a success, originally."),
   ("P3_TOM", "Fair enough. But the point is, with a success, everyone gives the credit to the product. With a failure, you can see which decisions actually mattered."),
   ("P3_LEAH", "And the founders published a really honest account of what went wrong afterwards, which is quite rare. That's what convinced me in the end."),
   ("P3_TUTOR", "What was the target?"),
   ("P3_TOM", "Ninety thousand pounds. They raised about fifty-one."),
   ("P3_TUTOR", "And the main reason, in your view?"),
   ("P3_LEAH", "Most commentators blamed the price. The basic pledge was sixty-five pounds, which is a lot for a board game. But when we went through the backers' comments, price came up surprisingly rarely. What came up again and again was shipping. The campaign page didn't say what delivery would cost outside the UK until the final week."),
   ("P3_TOM", "And over forty per cent of the page visits came from the US."),
   ("P3_TUTOR", "How are you measuring that, though? People who leave comments aren't a representative sample."),
   ("P3_TOM", "We know. So we've coded every comment by theme, but we're also comparing the daily pledge graph with the date the shipping table went up."),
   ("P3_LEAH", "There's a clear drop in new pledges right after it was posted, and cancellations jumped."),
   ("P3_TUTOR", "That's far stronger evidence than the comments on their own. I'd lead with that."),
   ("P3_TUTOR", "What about the video? Campaign videos often get the blame."),
   ("P3_LEAH", "We expected it to be a weakness, actually, because it's quite long. But the figures in the founders' account show that people watched it right to the end at a much higher rate than average."),
   ("P3_TOM", "So we're going to say the video wasn't a factor."),
   ("P3_TUTOR", "I'd soften that to: there's no evidence it was a factor. Now, for a comparison, don't choose the record-breaking campaign of that year. That's a different universe. And I know the same founders relaunched later and succeeded, but they changed too many things at once to isolate anything. Find a campaign priced at roughly the same level that published its shipping costs on day one."),
